{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "תשרפון", :translit "tisrefun", :gloss "you shall burn"} {:he "ואשריהם תשרפון", :translit "ve'asheirhem tisrefun", :gloss "and their asherahs you shall burn"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["תשרפון"]}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:7–8 discusses the rabbinic classification of three types of asherah-trees, distinguishing those that must be burned from those that may be stripped of their idolatrous use. Ba'al HaTurim links the plural formulation 'their asherahs you shall burn' to this threefold typology of asherahs.", :sources ["Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:7" "Mishnah Avodah Zarah 3:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ואבדתם את שמם", :translit "u'vi'adetem et shemam", :gloss "and you shall destroy their name"} {:he "לא תעשון כן", :translit "lo ta'asun khen", :gloss "you shall not do so"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Phrase לא תעשון כן from Deuteronomy 12:31 read as a prohibition against erasing God's Name."}], :frame {:text "Makkot 22a interprets the phrase לא תעשון כן in Deuteronomy 12:31 as a prohibition directed at one who would erase God's Name, reading 'so you shall not do' as 'you shall not do thus to My Name.' Ba'al HaTurim applies this derivation to the command 'you shall destroy their name' in Deuteronomy 12:3, explaining that destroying the names of idols is commanded precisely because one must not do the equivalent to God's own Name.", :sources ["Makkot 22a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["תשרפון"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "תשרפון", :refs ["Deuteronomy 7:5" "Deuteronomy 7:25" "Deuteronomy 12:3"], :n 3, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Phrase לא תעשון כן from Deuteronomy 12:31 read as a prohibition against erasing God's Name.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:04.249418274Z", :model "glm-5.2"}